col3:
We examine the potential of a neutrino factory for determining mixing angles, the CP-violating phase, and mass-squared differences by observing wrong-sign muons from the chain \( \mu^+ 	o 
u_e 	o 
u_\mu 	o \mu^- \) and right-sign muons from \( \mu^+ 	o  ar{
u}_\mu 	o  ar{
u}_\mu 	o \mu^+ \) (analogous to \( \mu^- \) chains), where \( 
u_e 	o 
u_\mu \) and \(  ar{
u}_\mu 	o  ar{
u}_\mu \) represent neutrino oscillation channels over a long baseline. Initially, we optimize the baseline and energy for the neutrino factory, incorporating recent simulation outcomes from the magnetized iron neutrino detector (MIND). Next, we explore physics using near detectors and address the handling of systematic uncertainties, such as cross-section errors, flux errors, and background variations. Finally, we analyze the impacts of an extra massive sterile neutrino with combined near and far detector setups.
